& [Intent]
  + join the already proven unmodified llama.cpp two-checkpoint tool-reflection flow to the already proven Slice10 volatile lifecycle-custody MCP
  + measure whether host-owned pre-registration plus a compact validation handle reduces repeated inference traffic while preserving the exact lifecycle response
  + establish one runnable local experiment rather than modify llama.cpp or claim a shared hidden-state or mid-token inference mechanism

& [GovernanceBoundary]
  + this file preserves the proposed experiment input and is not canonical specification implementation authority or permission to execute it
  + process this source through SJS before implementation
  + retain the closed Slice7 lifecycle semantics Slice8 stateless adapter semantics Slice9 registry semantics and Slice10 volatile custody semantics unchanged

& [PublicFixture]
  + move the complete deterministic lifecycle request construction out of private integration-test helper status into one separately versioned sanitized fixture generator or checked-in request artifact
  + identify every fixture by a stable fixture name canonical serialized byte count and digest
  + provide at least one lifecycle-valid fixture and one well-formed retained request whose lifecycle result is refused
  + construct proof-bearing signatures trust context receipts and verification facts deterministically on the host and never ask the model to invent them
  + prove that the public fixture produces the same core response as the existing Slice7 direct-validation fixture

& [HostBridge]
  + use the pinned local llama.cpp release model alias and two-checkpoint OpenAI-compatible flow already recorded by the llama_tool_reflection experiment
  + start one Slice10 stdio MCP subprocess and use its official protocol surface rather than call custody internals
  + pre-register the selected fixture directly from the trusted experiment host
  + expose to the model one bounded OpenAI-style function whose arguments are the exact compact validation handle
  + translate exactly one validated assistant tool call into the MCP VALIDATE command
  + append the matching tool result with the original tool_call_id and request a second completion with tool_choice none
  + ask the second checkpoint to report only a small declared projection of lifecycle stage disposition and source identity rather than echo the full response

& [MeasurementArms]
  + [A_stateless] send the complete Slice8 validation request on every measured repetition
  + [B_volatile_custody] register once outside measured steady state then send only the compact Slice10 validation handle on every measured repetition
  + run both arms against the same fixture model endpoint generation settings prompt and trial count
  + randomize or alternate arm order after one explicitly excluded warm-up per arm
  + record first-call and steady-state observations separately

& [Measurements]
  + exact semantic equality of the complete core lifecycle response between arms
  + serialized host-to-tool argument bytes tool-to-host response bytes prompt tokens completion tokens wall latency tool-call validity and second-checkpoint import validity
  + report byte compression independently from model-token reduction because host-owned registration can remove transport bytes without necessarily removing all prompt context
  + record provider release model file digest or immutable local identity endpoint command generation parameters timeout trial count hardware and timestamp
  + preserve raw bounded machine-readable observations and derive summaries without replacing them

& [RestartTrial]
  + terminate and restart the volatile custody process after one successful compact validation
  + prove the old handle refuses visibly in the fresh process
  + exclude restart behavior from steady-state averages and never describe volatile custody as persistence

& [InputAndOutputClosure]
  + deny unknown function names unknown MCP methods unknown command variants and unknown fields before semantic execution
  + accept exactly one tool call per checkpoint and reject parallel duplicate or malformed calls
  + bound serialized input output diagnostic and elapsed-time fields before retention
  + retain no model-private reasoning hidden state KV cache secrets credentials or unrelated prompts

& [Honesty]
  + a successful experiment establishes only the observed local tool-loop behavior under the recorded provider model fixtures and settings
  + exact semantic equality means byte-equivalent typed lifecycle outcomes after canonical serialization and does not imply factual truth safety permission or execution authority
  + a model-authored handle is only a lookup request and cannot create reconstruct alter or authorize lifecycle meaning
  + record invalid calls refusals timeouts and incomplete trials rather than silently retry them into apparent success

& [Security]
  + no filesystem network process build install signing admission deployment or execution capability is exposed to the model-facing function
  + the host may launch only the explicitly selected local llama-server and custody MCP processes needed by the bounded experiment
  + use no remote machine provider mutation OneDrive directory secret-bearing input or user work outside the experiment boundary
  + do not weaken Windows Application Control antivirus firewall or repository evidence gates

& [Acceptance]
  + fixture identity and digest lineage are independently reproducible
  + both measurement arms return exactly the same core response for every admitted comparison trial
  + valid and lifecycle-refused fixtures both complete the two-checkpoint import
  + malformed substituted unknown duplicate and restarted-handle cases refuse visibly
  + raw observations support every reported byte token latency and validity claim
  + focused debug optimized-release lint format evidence and repository-diff gates pass

& [Locked]
  + no llama.cpp source modification hidden-state injection KV-cache sharing mid-token semantic insertion remote provider call remote machine deployment FPGA implementation durable custody authentication authorization production hardening or general-purpose agent orchestration

& [OpenInputsForSJS]
  + select whether the public fixture is generated at runtime or checked in as canonical serialized data
  + select the local endpoint and confirm it is live before execution
  + select a bounded trial count timeout and projection schema based on a preflight measurement
